  "assessment": {
    "rationale": "Clear envelope/payload separation and explicit dispatch failure make this a plausible transport-neutral wrapper above UDP-feed, but the draft does not define the actual UDP-feed binding or the session semantics needed to prove composition without transport-detail leakage.",
    "strengths": [
      "Strong layer boundary: pcid selects interpretation, payload stays opaque, and incompatible handling fails at dispatch.",
      "Canonical DAG-CBOR bytes and mandatory signature presence support durable local capture under sparse knowledge.",
      "No central registry assumption and cautious unknown-pcid salvage align with PromiseGrid goals."
    ],
    "weaknesses": [
      "No concrete UDP-feed v0 API mapping, so the scenario's core sufficiency question is only partially answered.",
      "Ordering, replay, fragmentation, and group/session behavior are delegated to other layers.",
      "Draft, unfrozen specimen; signature/authorship details remain external and signature substructure is unclear."
    ],
    "risks": [
      "Best-effort salvage of unknown payloads could be over-trusted despite unsupported/unverified marking.",
      "Externalized signature semantics may fragment interoperability or hide security assumptions.",
      "Implementers may leak transport details when binding this envelope to UDP-feed because the boundary contract is unspecified."
    ],
    "open_questions": [
      "What exact UDP-feed v0 primitives are assumed to carry and recover these envelopes?",
      "What peer-local records make a received envelope sufficient session evidence for Alice, Bob, or Carol?",
      "Is the signature slot intended to stay fully opaque, or is a nested sig_pcid/sig_payload structure intended?"
    ],
    "authority_boundary": "Evidence only; does not settle PromiseGrid design."
  }
